figure('randspat', RF / 'Fig3_random_vs_spatial_cv_v1.png', 'Mean ROC-AUC under random 5-fold cross-validation and spatial block cross-validation (81 km blocks), with the same corrected code. The dotted line marks chance level.')
para(f'Under spatial validation, CBPP was the most predictable disease (ROC-AUC about {fm("CBPP", "(a) Rank average"):.2f}) and LSD the least (about {fm("LSD", "(a) Rank average"):.2f}). Fold-mean PR-AUC was above its no-skill level for every model, but only slightly for FS1 on FMD ({fm("FMD", "FS1", "PR_AUC"):.3f} against a prevalence of {prev["FMD"] / 100:.3f}). Choosing one model by inner-fold ROC-AUC (b) was never better than the rank average, which agrees with the selection-bias argument of Cawley and Talbot {{Cawley2010}}. Among the 23 library models, the best fold-mean ROC-AUC was {lib_mean["CBPP"].max():.3f} for CBPP ({lib_best["CBPP"]}), {lib_mean["FMD"].max():.3f} for FMD ({lib_best["FMD"]}) and {lib_mean["LSD"].max():.3f} for LSD ({lib_best["LSD"]}) (Supplementary Table S4).')
slope_rng = lambda d: (min(fold_slope[(d, m)] for m in MODELS), max(fold_slope[(d, m)] for m in MODELS))
pool_rng = lambda d: (min(pool_slope[(d, m)][0] for m in MODELS), max(pool_slope[(d, m)][0] for m in MODELS))
bss_rng = lambda d: (min(bss[(d, m)][0] for m in MODELS), max(bss[(d, m)][0] for m in MODELS))
para(f'Calibration differed between the two views ({T("cal")}). Within single test folds, the median calibration slope was {slope_rng("FMD")[0]:.2f}-{slope_rng("FMD")[1]:.2f} for FMD and {slope_rng("LSD")[0]:.2f}-{slope_rng("LSD")[1]:.2f} for LSD, so the probabilities within a fold were too close to the average risk. On the pooled predictions, the slopes were lower ({pool_rng("FMD")[0]:.2f} to {pool_rng("FMD")[1]:.2f} for FMD and {pool_rng("LSD")[0]:.2f} to {pool_rng("LSD")[1]:.2f} for LSD), which suggests that the overall level of the predictions did not follow the differences in prevalence between folds. For CBPP both views gave slopes close to 1. The Brier skill score was {z2(bss_rng("CBPP")[0])} to {z2(bss_rng("CBPP")[1])} for CBPP, {z2(bss_rng("FMD")[0])} to {z2(bss_rng("FMD")[1])} for FMD and {z2(bss_rng("LSD")[0])} to {z2(bss_rng("LSD")[1])} for LSD. The LSD probabilities were therefore no better than predicting the prevalence, and for FMD and LSD the predicted probabilities should be used for ranking, not as absolute risks (calibration plots in Supplementary Figures S2 and S7).')
rows = [[d, m.replace(' Rank average', '').replace(' Inner-selected single', ''), c['Calibration slope: fold median (IQR)'], c['Calibration slope: pooled [95% CI]'], c['Calibration intercept: pooled [95% CI]'], c['Brier: pooled [95% CI]'], c['Reference Brier p(1-p)'], c['Brier skill score [95% CI]']]
        for d in DIS for m in MODELS for c in [cal(d, m)]]
