add('h2', '4.2 Feature ablation')
r = t7('FS5 minus FS1', 'FMD'); rcb, rl = t7('FS5 minus FS1', 'CBPP'), t7('FS5 minus FS1', 'LSD')
para(f'The full engineered set improved FMD prediction ({T("abl")}, {T("pair")}). The fold-mean gain of FS5 over FS1 was {ci_flat(r["Overall: fold mean [corrected-t 95% CI]"]).replace(", 95% CI", " (corrected t 95% CI")}; Holm-adjusted p = {r["Overall: Holm p"]:.3f} across the three diseases), FS5 was better in {r["Overall: folds > 0"]} folds, and the pooled estimate was {ci_txt(r["Overall: pooled [bootstrap 95% CI]"]).replace("95% CI", "bootstrap 95% CI")}. For CBPP, FS5 gave no gain ({rcb["Overall: fold mean [corrected-t 95% CI]"]}). For LSD, the gain was small and uncertain ({rl["Overall: fold mean [corrected-t 95% CI]"]}). On the held-out confirmatory partition (Section 3.5), the FMD gain was {fmd_conf["H1 FS5 - FS1: pooled"]:+.3f} (pooled bootstrap 95% CI {fmd_conf["H1 FS5 - FS1: CI_lo"]:+.3f} to {fmd_conf["H1 FS5 - FS1: CI_hi"]:+.3f}; FS5 better in {fmd_conf["H1 FS5 - FS1: folds better"]} folds; fold-level corrected t-test p = {fmd_conf["H1 FS5 - FS1: p_corrected"]:.3f}), and the LSD gain was {S9.loc["LSD", "H1 FS5 - FS1: pooled"]:+.3f} (95% CI {S9.loc["LSD", "H1 FS5 - FS1: CI_lo"]:+.3f} to {S9.loc["LSD", "H1 FS5 - FS1: CI_hi"]:+.3f}). H1 required a gain for both diseases, so it was not confirmed. The FMD estimate agrees in direction and size with the development result, but its fold-level test did not reach significance, and the hypotheses were fixed after the development results were known (Supplementary Table S7).')
pc = lambda s: inc(s, 'FMD', 'Pooled [bootstrap 95% CI]')
para(f'The ablation shows where the FMD gain comes from ({F("abl")}). Adding the climate indices raised the fold-mean ROC-AUC by {ci_txt(inc("FS2 - FS1", "FMD"))} and adding the coordinates by {ci_txt(inc("FS3 - FS2", "FMD"))}. These corrected t-intervals include zero, but the pooled bootstrap intervals of both steps excluded it ({pc("FS2 - FS1").replace(" [", ", 95% CI ").replace(", +", " to +").replace(", -", " to -").rstrip("]")} for climate and {pc("FS3 - FS2").replace(" [", ", 95% CI ").replace(", +", " to +").replace(", -", " to -").rstrip("]")} for coordinates). Adding the 18 neighbourhood and cross-disease rates after the coordinates changed it by only {ci_txt(inc("FS4 - FS3", "FMD"))}, and the sampling-density terms by {ci_txt(inc("FS5 - FS4", "FMD"))}. No single step was significant after Holm correction across the 12 steps, which is expected when a gain of {fmd_gain:.2f} is split into four parts. For CBPP no step changed ROC-AUC by more than {max(abs(inc_m[(s, "CBPP")]) for s in AI.Step.unique()):.3f}. For LSD, adding the rates lowered the within-year ROC-AUC from {float(ab("LSD", "FS3", "Within-year AUC fold mean")):.3f} to {float(ab("LSD", "FS4", "Within-year AUC fold mean")):.3f} (difference {ci_flat(inc("FS4 - FS3", "LSD", "Within-year fold mean [corrected-t 95% CI]"))}), which suggests that for LSD the rates carry between-campaign rather than within-campaign information (Section 4.6). Full results are in Supplementary Tables S15 and S16.')
